{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:15:38.940Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 3 is complete.\n\n**Implementation** — `src/core/status/dispatch-session.ts`\n- Exports `runCardSession`, `CardSessionOptions`, `CardInput`, `Launcher`.\n- Private `CardSession` class keeps the run loop under the function budget.\n- Derives ordered items, applies in-session set-aside ordering, shows `formatCardScreen`, reads cards via `readDispatchCard`.\n- Keys print `── <label> ──` / `── exit <code> ──`, launch the command, then re-derive; reject asks `Reason: ` and appends the answer as one argument (empty/null skips the launch).\n- Caches one pending `input.key()` across waiting and the first card.\n- Empty inbox prints the waiting line, uses `watchDispatch`, closes it on first arrival, calls `sound.notify(at)` once, and never sounds while a card is open.\n- `q`, `\\u0003`, null, or `signal` abort exit; the watch and abort listener are released in `finally`.\n\n**Tests** — `tests/dispatch-session.test.ts` (13 tests, all Card session scenarios) using scripted input, a marker-writing recording launcher, a recording sound, a fake watcher, an immediate debounce scheduler, and a manual `every` timer.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/dispatch-session.test.ts` → 13/13 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` → passes (typechecks, build, full suite, lint).\n\nOne deviation noted in the result: `tests/no-skipped-in-src.test.ts` forbids the word \"skipped\" under `src/`, so the implementation uses \"set aside\" internally while matching the delta's behavior.\n\n`openspec/changes/099-inbox-cards/.run/results/3.md` written."}}
